{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening. I'm Dr. ___. You're here because of flank pain and a possible infection. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:15:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had pain on both sides, worse on the left. Feels just like when I get pyelo—same sharp pain, worse when I breathe. I had a fever last night, 101.2."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:16:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just nausea, but I think it’s from being anxious. Urine’s been cloudy and smells bad. No blood though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:18:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll run some tests—blood work, urine, and an ultrasound. Given your history, we’re concerned about a kidney infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. I usually end up septic. I’ve got a stent on the left side—could that be blocked again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2145-02-28 01:20:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s possible. The ultrasound will help us see if there’s hydronephrosis. We’ll also check your kidney function and start antibiotics if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are back. White count is elevated at 12.4—sign of infection. Creatinine is 3.3, which is your baseline. Urinalysis shows bacteria and white cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s another UTI? What about the stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely pyelonephritis. The ultrasound shows moderate to severe left hydronephrosis—your stent may be blocked. We’ve consulted urology and infectious disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They’ll replace the stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:36:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’re planning to exchange it. In the meantime, we’re starting IV antibiotics. Because of your allergies, we’re using tobramycin and daptomycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember tobramycin from last time. Is it safe with my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2145-02-28 08:38:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your kidney function closely. It’s effective for your typical infections, including E. coli and Enterococcus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2145-03-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day for your stent exchange. It’s scheduled for 12 PM. The radiology team will do it under imaging guidance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2145-03-03 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be awake?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2145-03-03 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get light sedation—fentanyl and midazolam—so you’ll be relaxed but breathing on your own. They’ll use a wire to guide the new stent in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2145-03-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure went well. They exchanged your left nephroureteral stent. The old one was partially blocked. The new one is 24 cm and positioned correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2145-03-03 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean the infection will clear up faster?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2145-03-03 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, relieving the blockage helps. We’re waiting on urine culture results to confirm which bacteria are involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2145-03-04 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The urine culture grew E. coli, Enterococcus, and Staph aureus—all sensitive to the antibiotics you’re on. No Pseudomonas this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2145-03-04 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So we’re on the right track?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2145-03-04 11:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll continue tobramycin and daptomycin for two weeks. We placed a midline for IV access since you can’t have a PICC due to allergies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2145-03-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is improving, and you’re running no fever. Creatinine is stable. We uncapped your nephrostomy tube yesterday to help drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2145-03-05 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I noticed more output. Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2145-03-05 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It means your kidney is draining better. We’ll recapture it once we’re sure function is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2145-03-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re placing a midline today to make giving antibiotics easier. It’s a temporary IV in your upper arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2145-03-06 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it like a PICC?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2145-03-06 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Shorter and doesn’t go as far. Safer for you given your allergy history. You’ll keep it until antibiotics are done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2145-03-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium is low—132. You’ve been drinking a lot of Gatorade, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2145-03-07 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, 3 or 4 a day. I like the taste and I’m trying to flush things out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2145-03-07 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely why your sodium dropped. Too much fluid can dilute your blood. We recommend cutting back to 2 liters a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2145-03-07 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that affect my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2145-03-07 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s actually better. Your creatinine went down to 2.9 when you drank more, but now we want balance. We’ll monitor both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2145-03-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sodium is back to 138. Good job cutting down. Creatinine is 3.4—still in your baseline range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2145-03-08 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m stable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2145-03-08 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We recapped the nephrostomy tube yesterday. Your kidney is handling drainage on its own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2145-03-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re halfway through antibiotics. No fever, pain is mild. We’re on track for a full two-week course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2145-03-09 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I go home on IV meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2145-03-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tried to set up home infusion, but it didn’t work out. And you didn’t want to go to a skilled nursing facility?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2145-03-09 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’d rather stay here if I have to. I’m comfortable with the team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2145-03-09 10:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you here to finish the IV antibiotics. Midline will stay in until the last dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2145-03-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All signs point to the infection clearing. We’ll continue monitoring labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2145-03-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Nephrostomy tube is staying in for now. You’ll need to keep it until your urology follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2145-03-11 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When is that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2145-03-11 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In about three months for routine exchange. But you need to see Dr. ___ within two weeks of discharge to discuss the stricture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2145-03-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One week left on antibiotics. Creatinine stable at 3.4. Sodium normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2145-03-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling much better. Can I start moving around more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2145-03-13 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re cleared for out-of-bed activity with assistance. Wheelchair or chair is fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2145-03-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Five more days of antibiotics. We’ll remove the midline before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2145-03-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Almost done. You’ve completed 13 days of tobramycin and daptomycin. One more dose tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2145-03-15 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And then I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2145-03-15 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll go home with your nephrostomy tube in place. Keep it capped unless instructed otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2145-03-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final antibiotic dose given. Midline removed. You’re infection-free and stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2145-03-16 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2145-03-16 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call Dr. ___ within two weeks. Also, get a Chem 7 blood test in a few days to check sodium and creatinine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2145-03-16 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2145-03-16 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep it in. Don’t remove it. Dr. ___ will decide when it can come out or be exchanged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2145-03-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge is set for tomorrow morning. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2145-03-17 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2145-03-17 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure you have all instructions and contacts before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2145-03-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Remember: follow up with urology, get your labs done, and keep the nephrostomy tube in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2145-03-18 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2145-03-18 08:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if you develop fever, pain, or swelling. Otherwise, see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2145-03-18 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2145-02-28 01:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2145-03-18 11:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with acute pyelonephritis and bilateral flank pain, consistent with his recurrent urinary tract infections. He has a history of T12 paraplegia, neurogenic bladder, ileal conduit, and chronic kidney disease. Imaging revealed moderate to severe left hydronephrosis, prompting a nephroureteral stent exchange on 2145-03-03. Urine cultures grew E. coli, Enterococcus, and Staph aureus, and due to multiple drug allergies, he was treated with IV tobramycin and daptomycin for two weeks. A midline was placed for antibiotic administration, as home infusion could not be arranged and the patient declined skilled nursing facility placement. During admission, he developed hyponatremia from excessive fluid intake, which resolved with fluid restriction. His kidney function remained within baseline, and the nephrostomy tube was recapped prior to discharge. He was discharged home with the nephrostomy tube in place, advised to follow up with urology within two weeks and to complete outpatient lab work to monitor renal and electrolyte status.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pyelonephritis without lesion of renal medullary necrosis",
      "Paraplegia",
      "Chronic kidney disease, Stage IV (severe)",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hyponatremia",
      "Hydronephrosis",
      "Escherichia coli infection",
      "Staphylococcus aureus infection",
      "Enterococcus infection",
      "Neurogenic bladder",
      "Chronic pain",
      "Anxiety"
    ]
  }
}
